Yes, we offer dedicated business enterprise plans that include a formal 99.9% uptime SLA. These plans are available under our Enterprise AirFiber tier; you can request more information by emailing enterprise-sales@airfiber.in.  

Source: AirFiber provides residential broadband plans (AirFiber 599, 1199, 1999). Dedicated business enterprise plans with formal 99.9% uptime SLAs are available under our Enterprise AirFiber tier by contacting enterprise-sales@airfiber.in.", "latency_ms": 1139.09, "tokens_used": 460, "prompt_tokens": 275, "completion_tokens": 185}

{"tool": "generate_ticket_reply", "reply": "[Ticket #T003]  
An official speed test for a refund claim must be performed using the official AirFiber Desktop App **or** via speed.airfiber.in, with the testing device connected **directly to the ONT via Ethernet**. You need to run **three consecutive tests**, spaced **one hour apart**.  

Source: Refund Policy document.", "latency_ms": 2844.3, "tokens_used": 421, "prompt_tokens": 266, "completion_tokens": 155}

{"tool": "generate_ticket_reply", "reply": "[Ticket #T016]  
A refund is available only if both of the following conditions are met: the request is made within the first 30 days after activation, and the service has a persistent speed drop below 50 % of the promised speed that cannot be resolved within 48 hours.  

Source: Refund Policy.", "latency_ms": 2880.64, "tokens_used": 419, "prompt_tokens": 263, "completion_tokens": 156}

{"tool": "generate_ticket_reply", "reply": "[Ticket #T022]  
To close your account, please return the ONT device and its power adapter within 14 days. If you keep the ONT, a fee of ₹2,500 applies, and ₹1,500 for any mesh extender not returned. Your ₹1,000 security deposit will be refunded within 7 days after we receive the equipment.  

[Source: Account Closure Policy]", "latency_ms": 984.06, "tokens_used": 509, "prompt_tokens": 295, "completion_tokens": 214}

{"tool": "generate_ticket_reply", "reply": "[Ticket #T073]  
A solid (non‑flashing) orange LED on your ONT means it is either in firmware‑update mode or detecting a degraded optical signal (approximately –27 dBm to –30 dBm). Please wait about 10 minutes; if the orange light remains solid, perform a single power‑cycle of the device.  

Source: Troubleshooting guide – solid orange LED indicates firmware update mode or degraded optical signal; wait 10 minutes, then power‑cycle if unchanged.", "latency_ms": 2648.88, "tokens_used": 475, "prompt_tokens": 275, "completion_tokens": 200}

{"tool": "generate_ticket_reply", "reply": "[Ticket #T118]  
I understand how frustrating a 2‑day outage can be, especially after three months of service. According to our Refund Policy, full plan refunds are only available within the first 30 days of activation. Since your service has been active for 3 months, a full refund isn’t applicable. However, you do qualify for a pro‑rata billing credit of ₹100 for each outage day, which would be ₹200 after verification. Please let us know if you’d like to proceed with the credit claim.  

*Source: Refund Policy*", "latency_ms": 949.88, "tokens_used": 574, "prompt_tokens": 276, "completion_tokens": 298}

